# Backups for the patente database.
#
# The live database is inside the Coolify volume rboj5u2xk5dj4o4yto89ablh_patente-data,
# not on the host filesystem. This job used to point at /srv/patente/patente.db — the
# retired systemd deployment — which meant the real data went unprotected while a backup
# ran green every night against the wrong database. That is the worst shape a backup can
# take, and it is why the script now asserts WHICH database it got rather than only that
# the file is valid SQLite.
#
# HOURLY, not daily. The RPO is the whole point: at daily, a disk failure at 02:00 costs a
# day of progress, entitlement and paid-for generated content. The run takes seconds and
# each snapshot is ~2.7 MB, so the tighter window costs nothing.
#
# Retention is tiered (ops/prune.py): hourly for two days, daily for a month, weekly for a
# quarter, monthly for a year — about 93 files and 250 MB, covering 333 days. Flat
# retention at this cadence would cover two and a half days.
#
# The WATCHDOG is a separate entry running a separate file on purpose: a script that
# alerts on its own failure cannot alert when it never runs at all. Offset to :40 so it
# checks after the hourly run has had time to finish.
#
# Alerts go to Telegram, configured in /etc/patente-backup.env (mode 600, not in git).
# MAILTO is left set but is not the mechanism — postfix here is loopback-only with no
# relayhost and /var/mail has never been written, so cron mail goes nowhere.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MAILTO=root

0  * * * * root /usr/local/sbin/patente-backup >> /var/log/patente-backup.log 2>&1
40 * * * * root /usr/local/sbin/patente-backup-watchdog >> /var/log/patente-backup.log 2>&1
